rder="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133371813.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A visionary mother and daughter duo transformed sustainability into an art form, building a seven-room home out of more than 8,000 recycled glass bottles. Incorporating elements like reclaimed wood and toothpaste tubes, this remarkable endeavor addresses the dual challenges of beach pollution and housing shortages in Brazil. Named the Salt House, it stands as a sustainable residence and an inspiring venue for community education on environmental responsibility and innovative reuse.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-a-brazilian-mother-and-daughter-began-collecting-discarded-bottles-years-later-more-than-8000-glass-bottles-had-become-the-walls-of-their-seven-bedroom-home-that-glows-during-sunrise/articleshow/133371813.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-a-brazilian-mother-and-daughter-began-collecting-discarded-bottles-years-later-more-than-8000-glass-bottles-had-become-the-walls-of-their-seven-bedroom-home-that-glows-during-sunrise/articleshow/133371813.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T16:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133371883,imgsize-141907.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US's secret Hormuz corridor: How America kept ships and oil moving despite closure]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133374684.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/uss-secret-hormuz-corridor-how-america-kept-ships-and-oil-moving-despite-closure/articleshow/133374684.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.