ross the country.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/americas-favourite-vegetable-could-be-hit-by-california-drought-over-90-of-fresh-broccoli-comes-from-the-state-while-severe-drought-may-cut-shipments-sharply/articleshow/133374389.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/americas-favourite-vegetable-could-be-hit-by-california-drought-over-90-of-fresh-broccoli-comes-from-the-state-while-severe-drought-may-cut-shipments-sharply/articleshow/133374389.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T18:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133374706,imgsize-107249.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1936, Beryl Markham Made History Flying the Atlantic Solo Westward]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133373726.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-1936-beryl-markham-took-off-from-england-alone-hoping-to-reach-new-york-20-hours-later-ice-starved-her-engine-and-she-crash-landed-in-canada-after-becoming-the-first-woman-to-fly-the-atlantic-solo-east-to-west/articleshow/133373726.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-1936-beryl-markham-took-off-from-england-alone-hoping-to-reach-new-york-20-hours-later-ice-starved-her-engine-and-she-crash-landed-in-canada-after-becoming-the-first-woman-to-fly-the-atlantic-solo-east-to-west/articleshow/133373726.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T15:54:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133373878,imgsize-807512.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Nathan Cofnas faces ‘appropriate action’ from Ghent University after Arday’s death]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133373842.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/nathan-cofnas-the-scholar-who-exposed-jason-ardays-plagiarism-faces-appropriate-action-from-ghent-university-after-ardays-death/articleshow/133373842.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/nathan-cofnas-the-scholar-who-exposed-jason-ardays-plagiarism-faces-appropriate-action-from-ghent-university-after-ardays-death/articleshow/133373842.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T15:58:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133374002,imgsize-1744305.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[For over 50 years, Elizabeth Dickens recorded Block Island's birds, creating a historic record]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133372163.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[For more than five decades, Elizabeth Dickens kept a detailed account of bird sightings on Block Island. Her comprehensive journals offered insights into local bird populations and their migratory habits while she inspired students through educational efforts about avian life. Dickens' commitment to her craft resulted in invaluable contributions to ornithology, emphasizing how crucial careful observation is for comprehending the natural world.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1912-a-rhode-island-woman-began-recording-every-days-bird-sightings-on-block-island-she-continued-for-more-than-50-years-and-left-behind-one-of-the-islands-longest-wildlife-records/articleshow/133372163.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1912-a-rhode-island-woman-began-recording-every-days-bird-sightings-on-block-island-she-continued-for-more-than-50-years-and-left-behind-one-of-the-islands-longest-wildlife-records/articleshow/133372163.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T16:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133372236,imgsize-110389.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Carl Linnaeus: "Human beings, having, above..."]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133373633.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Human reasoning provides us with a special lens through which we can observe and understand nature. This ability to study and reflect upon natural processes imposes an ethical responsibility on us to avoid exploiting the environment. By grasping the intricate connections within ecosystems, we appreciate our place in the natural world. The wisdom of Linnaeus serves as a guiding light for today's pressing ecological issues.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/quote-of-the-day-by-carl-linnaeus-human-beings-having-above-all-creatures-received-the-power-of-reason-need-to-be-/articleshow/133373633.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/quote-of-the-day-by-carl-linnaeus-human-beings-having-above-all-creatures-received-the-power-of-reason-need-to-be-/articleshow/133373633.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T15:46:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133373852,imgsize-108736.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[For the first time in history, astronauts use portable X-ray technology in space]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" al